{"id":"dag-cache-invalidation","t":"Pipeline cache keys and invalidation over a DAG","tags":["MLOps","Data Processing"],"d":"Medium","rt":"python","fn":"plan_run","tol":[1e-06,1e-08],"pkgs":[],"st":"An ML pipeline (prepare data, tokenize, train, evaluate, export) is a DAG of steps. An orchestrator can skip a step whose output already exists **for exactly the same inputs**. The usual trick is a **cache key**: a hash of the step's own code version and parameters together with the cache keys of the steps it depends on. A change anywhere upstream then changes every downstream key automatically.\n\nWrite `plan_run(steps, cache)`.\n\n- `steps`: a dict `name -> {\"deps\": [names], \"code\": str, \"params\": dict}`. The graph is acyclic and every dependency is a key of `steps`.\n- `cache`: a list of cache keys whose outputs already exist in the artifact store.\n\n## 1. Order\nReturn the steps in **topological order**: a step comes after all its dependencies. Among the steps that are ready at the same time, take the alphabetically smallest name first.\n\n## 2. Cache keys\nGoing through that order, the key of step `s` is the first 12 characters of the SHA-256 hex digest of the UTF-8 bytes of\n```python\njson.dumps({\"name\": s, \"code\": code, \"params\": params, \"deps\": dep_keys}, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n```\nwhere `dep_keys` is the list of the dependencies' keys, ordered by **dependency name** (so the order in `deps` does not matter).\n\n## 3. Plan\nA step must run if its key is not in `cache`. Return\n`{\"order\": [...], \"run\": [steps that must run, in topological order], \"keys\": {name: key}}`.","starter":"import hashlib\nimport json\n\ndef plan_run(steps, cache):\n    \"\"\"Return the topological order, the steps to run and every step's cache key.\"\"\"\n    order = sorted(steps)\n    keys = {}\n    for s in order:\n        blob = json.dumps({\"name\": s, \"code\": steps[s][\"code\"], \"params\": steps[s][\"params\"]}, sort_keys=True)\n        keys[s] = hashlib.sha256(blob.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:12]\n    run = [s for s in order if keys[s] not in cache]\n    return {\"order\": order, \"run\": run, \"keys\": keys}\n","hints":["Compute keys in topological order, so every dependency already has its key when you reach a step.","If a step's key ignores its dependencies, changing the tokenizer will not rerun training, and the \"cached\" model was trained on the old tokens.","For the order, keep the ready steps in a heap (`heapq`) and always pop the smallest name."],"sol":"import hashlib\nimport heapq\nimport json\n\ndef plan_run(steps, cache):\n    # Kahn's algorithm; a heap makes ties deterministic (smallest name first)\n    indeg = {s: len(set(spec[\"deps\"])) for s, spec in steps.items()}\n    children = {s: [] for s in steps}\n    for s, spec in steps.items():\n        for d in set(spec[\"deps\"]):\n            children[d].append(s)\n    ready = [s for s, k in indeg.items() if k == 0]\n    heapq.heapify(ready)\n    order = []\n    while ready:\n        s = heapq.heappop(ready)\n        order.append(s)\n        for c in children[s]:\n            indeg[c] -= 1\n            if indeg[c] == 0:\n                heapq.heappush(ready, c)\n\n    keys, have = {}, set(cache)\n    for s in order:                                   # deps are keyed before s, by construction\n        spec = steps[s]\n        dep_keys = [keys[d] for d in sorted(set(spec[\"deps\"]))]\n        blob = json.dumps({\"name\": s, \"code\": spec[\"code\"], \"params\": spec[\"params\"], \"deps\": dep_keys},\n                          sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"))\n        keys[s] = hashlib.sha256(blob.encode(\"utf-8\")).hexdigest()[:12]\n    run = [s for s in order if keys[s] not in have]\n    return {\"order\": order, \"run\": run, \"keys\": keys}\n","ex_md":"## Why the key must include upstream keys\nA cache key is a promise: \"this output was produced from exactly these inputs.\" The inputs of `train` include the tokenized data, so the key of `train` must change when anything that produced that data changes. Hashing the upstream **keys** (not their outputs, and not just their names) does this cheaply and transitively: test 3 changes only the tokenizer code and every step from `tokenize` down reruns, while `data` is reused.\n\n## Content addressing makes reverts free\nThe cache is a set of keys, not a \"latest output\" per step. Test 4 goes back to the original configuration after the tokenizer experiment, and nothing reruns, because the old outputs are still stored under their old keys. Test 2 changes one eval setting: only `eval_gsm` reruns, which is what makes cheap re-evaluation of a trained model possible.\n\n## Determinism\nBoth the order and the keys must be identical on every machine. Sorting the dependency keys by name removes dependence on how `deps` was written; `sort_keys=True` and fixed separators fix the JSON bytes; a heap fixes the tie order among ready steps. Adding a dependency (test 5) is a real change and does change the key.\n\n## Complexity\nTopological sort is $O(V + E)$ plus $O(V \\log V)$ for the heap; hashing is linear in the serialised size.\n\n## Where this breaks\nThe key covers only what you put in it. A step that reads \"the latest\" table, the current time or an unpinned package is not a pure function of its key, and caching it silently serves stale or wrong results. Pin those inputs (a snapshot ID, a lockfile hash) and include them in `params`, or disable caching for that step.","nex":2,"shown":[{"in":"{'data': {'deps': [], 'code': 'data-v3', 'params': {'snapshot': 'mix-v12'}}, 'tokenize': {'deps': ['data'], 'code': 'tok-v1', 'params': {'vocab': 65536}}, 'train': {'deps': ['tokenize'], 'code': 'train-v7', 'params': {'lr': 0.0003, 'steps': 20000}}, 'eval_gsm': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'eval-v2', 'params': {'shots': 8}}, 'eval_mmlu': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'eval-v2', 'params': {'shots': 5}}, 'export': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'export-v1', 'params': {'dtype': 'bf16'}}}\n[]","out":"{'order': ['data', 'tokenize', 'train', 'eval_gsm', 'eval_mmlu', 'export'], 'run': ['data', 'tokenize', 'train', 'eval_gsm', 'eval_mmlu', 'export'], 'keys': {'data': '991b11030d8d', 'tokenize': '8b90d07a9c9c', 'train': 'ef6e10d09056', 'eval_gsm': '0a04f841d2b1', 'eval_mmlu': '65c7c997736f', 'export': '312418a4b321'}}"},{"in":"{'data': {'deps': [], 'code': 'data-v3', 'params': {'snapshot': 'mix-v12'}}, 'tokenize': {'deps': ['data'], 'code': 'tok-v1', 'params': {'vocab': 65536}}, 'train': {'deps': ['tokenize'], 'code': 'train-v7', 'params': {'lr': 0.0003, 'steps': 20000}}, 'eval_gsm': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'eval-v2', 'params': {'shots': 4}}, 'eval_mmlu': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'eval-v2', 'params': {'shots': 5}}, 'export': {'deps': ['train'], 'code': 'export-v1', 'params': {'dtype': 'bf16'}}}\n['991b11030d8d', '8b90d07a9c9c', 'ef6e10d09056', '0a04f841d2b1', '65c7c997736f', '312418a4b321']","out":"{'order': ['data', 'tokenize', 'train', 'eval_gsm', 'eval_mmlu', 'export'], 'run': ['eval_gsm'], 'keys': {'data': '991b11030d8d', 'tokenize': '8b90d07a9c9c', 'train': 'ef6e10d09056', 'eval_gsm': '69c9fe4c6c90', 'eval_mmlu': '65c7c997736f', 'export': '312418a4b321'}}"}],"lessons":[{"href":"/self-learning-tracks/library/ai-research-track-web/mlops/pipelines-and-orchestration/","t":"Pipelines and orchestration","c":"AI Research"}],"related":["topologically-sort-computation-dag","content-hash-data-manifest","retry-backoff-schedule"],"theory":[{"lesson":"air-fanout-v1:14.04","step":null,"label":"Pipelines and orchestration","href":"/self-learning-tracks/library/ai-research-track-web/mlops/pipelines-and-orchestration/"}],"ntests":7,"tj":"[{\"a\": [{\"__dict__\": [[\"data\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"deps\", []], [\"code\", \"data-v3\"], [\"params\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"snapshot\", \"mix-v12\"]]}]]}], [\"tokenize\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"deps\", [\"data\"]], [\"code\", \"tok-v1\"], [\"params\", {\"__dict__\": [[\"vocab\", 65536]]}]]}], [\"train\", {\"